## Why This Is Asked

This question tests ability to design cost-aware prompt orchestration, a practical constraint in cloud analytics workflows.

## Key Concepts

- Token cost estimation
- Budget-constrained orchestration
- Module selection strategy
- Latency-awareness

## Code Example

```javascript
function estimateTokens(prompt, overhead = 20) {
  return prompt.split(/\s+/).length + overhead;
}

function selectModules(prompt, budget, candidates) {
  let total = 0;
  const chosen = [];
  for (const [name, cost] of candidates) {
    if (total + cost <= budget) {
      chosen.push(name);
      total += cost;
    }
  }
  return chosen;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you refine costs with real model pricing?
- How handle dynamic budgets or partial module failures?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses the ability to design intelligent, cost-aware routing systems for multi-module AI architectures in real-time environments, requiring consideration of performance trade-offs, safety constraints, and practical implementation details.

## Key Concepts

- Latency budgeting and real-time performance optimization
- Cost-aware routing and resource allocation
- Safety gating and data sensitivity handling
- Modular prompt orchestration and fallback mechanisms
- Policy-based decision making with precedence rules

## Code Example

```javascript
function routePrompt(prompt, signals) {
  const { budget, latency, safety, data_sensitivity } = signals;

  // Safety-first routing
  if (data_sensitivity > 0.7 || safety > 0.5) {
    return {
      module: 'SafetyGuard',
      plan: ['analyze_content', 'apply_filters', 'return_sanitized'],
      payload: { prompt, safety_score: safety, sensitivity_level: data_sensitivity }
    };
  }

  // Cost-optimized routing
  if (budget < 0.3 || latency < 100) {
    return {
      module: 'LightSummarizer',
      plan: ['extract_key_points', 'generate_summary'],
      payload: { prompt, max_tokens: 150 }
    };
  }

  // Default to comprehensive processing
  return {
    module: 'CitationEmbedder',
    plan: ['analyze_content', 'extract_citations', 'generate_embeddings'],
    payload: { prompt, include_sources: true }
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical prompt versioning and drift handling with concrete routing decisions for enterprise data assistants.

## Key Concepts
- Drift detection via keyword overlap scoring
- Baseline prompt management with patch generation
- Three-tier routing: Intent-Detector, Safety-Guard, Response-Composer
- Signal tracking: intent, data_sensitivity, version_delta
- Edge case handling: renamed intents, missing baselines

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for drift detection and routing
function routePrompt(newPrompt, baselinePrompt) {
  const overlap = calculateKeywordOverlap(newPrompt, baselinePrompt);
  const hasSafetyIssues = detectSafetyKeywords(newPrompt);

  if (hasSafetyIssues) return 'Safety-Guard';
  if (overlap < 0.6) return 'Intent-Detector';
  return 'Response-Composer';
}
```

